  "findings": [
    "Hybrid passed development eligibility separately from failing the playing-strength screen. Baseline selected epoch zero and did not pass development eligibility.",
    "Hybrid produced about 3.7 times as many fresh games in slightly less collection wall time; a cheap-data throughput improvement is established for this implementation and hardware.",
    "The small development improvement appears in every generation stratum but is checkpoint-selection evidence. No independent offline audit or confidence-gated strength confirmation was run.",
    "Baseline inference tensors exactly equal the generation-3 parent; the screen therefore compares the new hybrid evaluator against the unchanged parent inference function within this research search package.",
    "Both fits reduce training loss while later development loss worsens. These observations do not establish insufficient model capacity or justify larger models.",
    "A near-even exploratory screen with a negative mean-margin estimate is inconclusive about small strength effects and does not qualify for advancement; no confirmation was correctly started.",
    "Collection wall cost was matched within the prespecified tolerance; hybrid fitting cost more and sample count changes optimizer updates per epoch. This is not a pure data-quality effect at identical end-to-end compute.",
    "The fixed actor and current residual targets do not by themselves create an improving teacher iteration loop. Faster collection alone has not produced a stronger replacement teacher."
  ],
  "recommendations": [
    "Retain frozen generation 3 as the teacher; archive this hybrid checkpoint and preserve all negative screen results.",
    "Prioritize improving cheap generator decision quality over network width: a next bounded, separately frozen study can spend its same search fraction on early/pivotal decisions rather than random decisions, with costs recalibrated before outcomes.",
    "Use existing development and action diagnostics to choose one generator change; do not use the failed screen to tune or extend the same test.",
    "Keep identical pooled development and explicit replay masses; require fresh playing strength before making a cheaper collector checkpoint the next teacher.",
    "Do not interpret the 40-pair failed screen as proof the hybrid corpus is harmful or as proof cheap-data learning cannot work."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Single generator comparison, optimization seed and selected checkpoint per arm; no variance across independent fit/corpus repetitions.",
    "Same rules implementation and catalog underlie collection and evaluation; seed separation does not certify game correctness.",
    "No raw features, observations, labels, individual game outcomes or local paths are included in this aggregate review."
  ]
